        "original_id": "8a62db7c-2c87-5d39-ac16-8bd550ef74df",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alfred Preis\n- Places: Pearl Harbor, Honolulu, Hawaii\n- Organizations: USS Arizona Memorial\n- Events: Attack on Pearl Harbor, Japanese surprise attack on Pearl Harbor\n- Concepts: memorial design symbolism\n\nFacts:\n- On December 7, 1941, the Japanese surprise attack on Pearl Harbor killed 1,177 sailors and Marines on the USS Arizona.\n- The USS Arizona Memorial at Pearl Harbor in Honolulu, Hawaii, marks the resting place of 1,102 of the 1,177 sailors and Marines killed on the USS Arizona and commemorates the events of December 7, 1941.\n- Alfred Preis designed the memorial with a sagging center and strong, vigorous ends to express initial defeat and ultimate victory.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
